    By default, ``jnp.nansum`` computes the sum of elements along the flattened
    array.

    >>> nan = jnp.nan
    >>> x = jnp.array([[3, nan, 4, 5],
    ...                [nan, -2, nan, 7],
    ...                [2, 1, 6, nan]])
    >>> jnp.nansum(x)
    Array(26., dtype=float32)

    If ``axis=1``, the sum will be computed along axis 1.

    >>> jnp.nansum(x, axis=1)
    Array([12.,  5.,  9.], dtype=float32)

